# Rust build artifacts
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Dioxus web build output
/ui/dist
/ui/.dioxus

# Packaged webapp
/target/webapp

# Node (Playwright E2E)
node_modules/
/e2e/test-results
/e2e/playwright-report
/e2e/.cache

# Local node data from test runs
/.freenet-test
/e2e/.nodes

# Local review notes
/codebase-report.md
/pr-mtrav.md
/address.md

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Never commit built contract WASM: it is a build output, and a stale copy
# silently changes contract keys. `cargo make build-contracts` regenerates it.
*.wasm

# The one exception, and it is the same rule read the other way round. The web
# container's key IS the app's public address, so its bytes must never change by
# accident — a dependency bump, a different machine, even a different $HOME is
# enough to move it. It is therefore a committed artifact, published as-is and
# never rebuilt for a release. See published-contract/README.md.
!published-contract/*.wasm

# The webapp publisher keys. Whoever holds one controls what that app URL
# serves, so they are local-only and never committed. The glob covers the
# rotated copies (.v2-<ts> and so on) left behind when publishing to a new
# address — those are private keys too.
.freenet-publisher.key*
.freenet-public/
.freechess-account
